id: pm-evidence-coalesced-source-verification
title: Verify shared citation sources once per check
description: "Coalesce source reads within an evidence check, preserving immutable provider-authorized snapshots and exposing counts without a persistent cache or new source authority."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: backlog-1021,coalesced-source
created_at: "2026-10-25T22:24:41.473Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T07:51:48.476Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Fifty citations into one unchanged document require one source read; A document changing during read never produces mixed revisions; Cancellation produces an explicit incomplete receipt; Typed SDK and compact TOON/JSON CLI, strict boundary validation, no-git real-data proof, npm and Bun CI release gates"
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T22:24:46.064Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: src/evidence.ts check and affected currently call checkCitation per citation; src/sources.ts provides coherent bounded snapshots but no per-check reuse. The pinned core item-metadata-cache stores native item metadata, not caller source bytes. Sibling pm-context file-focus and pm-brief consume tracker items and linked-file focus, without source-fragment snapshot authority. Existing SDK-adoption work owns output accounting and is reused. No duplicate coalescing item exists. Implement invocation-local provider/source snapshot promises (including refusals), preserve root/adapter authority, expose source reads and cancellation in budgeted receipts, and keep observations behind fresh SDK CAS checks. No import/export/sync, durable cache, status classification or journal is introduced."
  "2026-10-25T22:37:50.232Z",codex-agent,"Implemented invocation-local provider/source snapshot sharing in check and affected, immutable adapter copies, prompt cancellation with incomplete receipts, strict option bounds, guarded source-read counts, and revision-fenced recording. First targeted source/command/regression run: 28 passed. Eight package lifecycle interleavings preserved peer reviews on real non-git trackers; cancellation and foreign-state recording controls are being finalized. Public pm-changelog snapshot fa8a8a1d0af97797e6a34a78bdd6b9b30242378e: 197 items, 50 citations across 5 items into one 27794-byte document, exactly 1 source read, all 50 current. Bounded 800-token SDK check: 751 estimated tokens, 5 returned, 45 omitted; native CLI TOON 1800 bytes/450 estimated tokens and JSON 3002 bytes/751 estimated tokens. All 405 copied public files unchanged after read-only checks; no git executable available. No hosted or original tracker data was modified."
  "2026-10-25T22:51:51.863Z",codex-agent,"State model passed: seed 0x5eeda11, 500 four-operation sequences, 2000 operations, 6 exact-byte citation variants, 26 evidence revisions and 500 SDK readbacks preserving 20 native fields plus links, comments and relationships. Targeted linked test command passed 14/14 via pm test --run --progress; the tracker disables automatic result retention, so this comment preserves the receipt. Additional controls cover same-counter envelope replays, native-revision transaction identities and CLI cancellation listener cleanup. Function-only behavioral reverts against origin/main each produced exactly one failing regression: check, snapshot, packet, Store.mutate and Store.commit (5/5 controls), with every source byte restored. No import/export/sync path, journaled plan, shared lease, checkpoint or status-name classification is introduced. Existing SDK transactions, complete-list certification, native get, status-compatible items, RelationshipGraph, history verification and output-accounting helpers remain the authorities. CI now invokes the exact npm release:check script on Node 22 and 26 and the exact Bun release:check script on Node 26; all existing thresholds stay unchanged. Full gates will run in CI to avoid the saturated host."
  "2026-10-25T22:55:29.349Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed overlap against the installed current 2026.10.25 CLI as well as the pinned 2026.10.23 SDK: no source-snapshot/coalescing/citation API is exported by the current SDK, and item-metadata-cache still owns native item metadata and linked collections only. The package pin is unchanged. A final targeted control also proves that changes to caller-owned options during a read cannot redirect tracker writes, source roots, adapter authority or output bounds. Local typecheck, lint, zero-duplication and complete-docstring gates pass; documentation includes the stable public-data measurements and five behavioral revert controls."
  "2026-10-25T23:00:28.429Z",codex-agent,"PR opened ready for review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/pull/6. Exact code-head real-data and behavioral-revert reruns passed with unchanged public measurements and five isolated negative controls. Initial CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/actions/runs/40242540774 reached 100/100/100/100 coverage on Node 22 and 26; 104/105 tests passed in each matrix job. The sole failure was the existing workflow contract requiring a separately named identity audit step, even though the release script invokes it. Restoring that explicit step, retaining the full npm/Bun scripts and all thresholds. The reference model is also strengthened with independent Node SHA-256 byte hashes, exact retained text, review fields, provenance, timestamp validation and native comment preservation. CI remains required before completion; no gate failure is treated as approval."
  "2026-10-25T23:09:16.784Z",codex-agent,"Release matrix passed at fdffcb14338edf61906b109c2eaca3230f571bd0: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/actions/runs/40242890105. Exact npm release:check passed on Node 22 and 26; exact bun release:check passed on Node 26. Each gate ran 105/105 main tests and 2/2 packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx journeys, with 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 20 configured authored source files; zero omissions, skips or cancellations in the final suites. CodeQL also passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-evidence/actions/runs/40242890103. Final guard captures the expected envelope before source awaits, including SDK result-view refreshes; its real-tracker regression passed and its function-only late-capture negative control failed exactly once. Current linked targeted command passed 16/16 through pm test --run --progress; all six behavioral revert controls passed, with source bytes restored. Final typecheck, lint, zero-duplication, complete docstrings and append-only history prefix checks passed. This final guard and handoff receipt will receive another exact-head CI run before the PR summary is finalized. Sourcery review was quota-limited and CodeRabbit did not run automatically; neither is approval, and no review trigger or mention was posted. Existing remote mutation conformance remains tracked separately by pm-evidence-backend-conformance. No new CLI/SDK defect was filed; automatic linked-test receipt persistence is disabled by tracker policy, so command results are preserved in these comments and the PR."
  "2026-10-26T07:09:26.121Z",codex-agent,"Read-only review blocked PR 6: a source ancestor heading containing a tab is accepted by cite but rejected by verification ancestry validation, causing item-wide skipping. Reopened active work on the existing item. Plan: a single producer/consumer citation schema module; per-citation refusals that preserve valid siblings and malformed records; seeded 1000-plus-document Markdown/JSON round trips and mutation checks, including the exact tab ancestor case; behavioral revert controls and unchanged CI release gates. No thread replies, review triggers, merge or release."
  "2026-10-26T07:41:33.944Z",codex-agent,"Implemented one Zod runtime module for citation, selector, ancestry, descriptor, observation and check shapes; public types are inferred and SDK consumers can import the same schemas. Producers (cite/select/anchor/section ancestry/re-anchor/review) and verification now share those contracts. Source-derived strings preserve literal tabs, Unicode and source-size bounds, replacing the incorrect identifier limit. Verification parses the envelope independently and reports malformed/null/duplicate/wrong-owner entries by citationIndex; valid siblings still resolve and record through the shared SDK CAS path, preserving bad entry data. First seeded property pass: 1024 accepted Markdown/JSON documents, 73 deliberately ambiguous selector refusals, mutations 238 changed / 274 ambiguous / 256 missing / 256 current, 64 non-git trackers with SDK readback. Added selected headings beyond 4096 characters to the same generator for the final run. The exact review case and mixed malformed/valid sibling regressions pass. Eight function-only behavioral negative controls each failed exactly once, including restoring the legacy ancestry refusal and restoring item-wide validation; source bytes were restored. No review thread reply, mention, merge or release was posted."
  "2026-10-26T07:43:06.048Z",codex-agent,"Final linked property run passed 4/4 tests via pm test --run --only-last --progress: seed 0x26c17e, 1024 accepted documents (512 Markdown/512 JSON), 73 deliberately refused duplicate-heading selectors, 64 non-git SDK trackers, retained exact-byte SDK readbacks and independent SHA-256 checks. Mutations: 238 changed / 274 ambiguous / 256 missing / 256 current; zero foreign items. Coverage includes selected headings and pointer keys beyond 4096 characters as well as tab ancestry, CRLF, combining Unicode, confusables, emphasis/code and deep duplicate headings. Mixed malformed entries retain their data while valid siblings resolve and record; each refusal carries citationIndex, code and remedy. Prior targeted compatibility run passed 32/32; focused review/mixed/schema regressions pass 3/3. Eight behavioral function-only negative controls each failed once and restored all bytes, including legacy ancestry rejection and item-wide validation. Build, typecheck, lint, zero duplication and complete docstrings passed. Automatic pm test result persistence remains disabled; these receipts and PR validation preserve the results. The pinned pm SDK is unchanged; Zod is an exact production dependency solely for one inferred runtime schema. CI full release gates remain required before handoff."
  "2026-10-26T07:51:48.475Z",codex-agent,"Instrumented targeted compatibility suite passed 44/44 tests with 100/100/100/100 coverage across citation-schema, evidence, selectors, store and verification. The shared provider schema is reused by adapter-option validation too, so literal provider labels cannot encounter a separate identifier policy; the focused shared-schema control passed. Preparing the unchanged npm/Bun CI release matrix. The prior public-data one-read measurements and unrelated fleet work are preserved."
